.TH du 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
du \- how much space a directory tree uses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B du
[\fB\-asxdk\fR] [\fB\-l\fI levels\fR] [\fIdirectory\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B du
walks each
.I directory
and prints how much space its files take, in 512-byte blocks, deepest
first.  With no argument it starts at the current directory.
.PP
A file with more than one link is counted once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Report every file, not just directories.
.TP
.B \-s
Report only the total for each argument.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-d
Do not cross onto another filesystem.
.TP
.B \-k
Report kilobytes rather than 512-byte blocks.
.TP
.BI \-l " levels"
Report only to this depth below each argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# du -s /root
# du -k /usr/bin
# du -a . | sort -nr
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR ls (1),
.BR find (1)
